      "id": 1,
      "text": "Waynesville was platted in 1833, making it the oldest city in Pulaski County, and its downtown tells stories of early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitpulaskicounty.org/stories?rec_id=410",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name honors Revolutionary War general Anthony Wayne, with “ville” added to his nickname “Mad Anthony.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.theroute-66.com/waynesville.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A mural at 1413 Historic Route 66, painted by Ray Harvey, showcases 11 local landmarks and a Route 66 shield.",
